merate.","-  // Then match: for each pivot, leftContrib + rightContrib + pivotValue = rhs (mod p)","-  // So: rightContrib = rhs - leftContrib - pivotValue (mod p)","-","-  // The total press count = leftFreePresses + rightFreePresses + sum(pivotValues)","-  // We want to minimize this.","-","-  // For each left assignment, we know leftContrib[r] for each pivot r.","-  // For each right assignment, we know rightContrib[r] for each pivot r.","-  // The constraint is: pivotValue[r] = rhs[r] - leftContrib[r] - rightContrib[r] (mod p)","-  // And we want min over (left, right) of: leftPresses + rightPresses + sum_r pivotValue[r]","-","-  // We can group right results by their rightContrib vector and keep only the best","-  // (min rightPresses, then lex). Then for each left, compute the required pivotValues.","-","-  // But the search space for matching is still large. Let me think differently.","-","-  // For each left assignment, the contribution vector is a tuple of rank values in GF(p).","-  // For each right assignment, similarly. The pivot values are determined by:","-  //   pivot[r] = (rhs[r] - leftContrib[r] - rightContrib[r]) mod p","-  // Total = leftPresses + rightPresses + sum_r pivot[r]","-","-  // We can group right by rightContrib vector, and for each group keep the best right.","-  // Then for each left, iterate over all right groups.","-","-  // The number of distinct rightContrib vectors is at most modulus^rank, but in practice","-  // much less since rightCount free vars can produce at most modulus^rightCount vectors.","-","-  // With half ~= 12-20 free vars per side and modulus up to 97, this is still huge.","-  // We need a smarter approach.","-","-  // Key optimization: we don't need to enumerate ALL right assignments.","-  // We group by rightContrib vector and keep only the best (min presses, then lex).","-  // But building this map still requires enumerating all right assignments.","-","-  // With 20 free vars split into 10+10, modulus 97: 97^10 ≈ 7e19, way too many.","-","-  // Hmm. For the counter puzzle with large modulus, we need a fundamentally different approach.","-  // Let's use integer linear programming or branch-and-bound.","-","-  // Actually, let me reconsider the constraints. The problem says up to 40 buttons and 40 counters.","-  // The number of free variables = numVars - rank. In the worst case, rank could be low,","-  // giving many free variables. But in practice, with 40 equations and 40 unknowns over GF(p),","-  // the system is likely well-determined.","-","-  // For the counter puzzle, let's use a branch-and-bound approach that prunes based on","-  // the current total press count.","-","-  // Actually, I think the most practical approach is:","-  // 1. After RREF, identify free variables.","-  // 2. If numFree is small enough (say <= 10 for modulus 97, or <= 20 for modulus 2), enumerate.","-  // 3. For larger, use a smarter enumeration with early pruning.","-","-  // But wait - for modulus 97 with even 5 free variables, 97^5 = 8.6 billion. That's too many.","-","-  // Let me reconsider. For the counter puzzle, the optimization objective is to minimize","-  // total presses. Each free variable can be 0..modulus-1. The pivot variables are determined","-  // by the free variables. The total is: sum(free) + sum(pivots).","-","-  // Each pivot is a linear combination of free variables (plus constant). So the total","-  // is a linear function of the free variables over the integers (not mod p, because we're","-  // summing the actual values 0..p-1).","-","-  // Wait, not exactly. The pivot value is computed mod p, but we count it as the value","-  // in range 0..p-1. So it's: sum(free_i) + sum_r ((rhs_r - sum_j coeff[r][j]*free_j) mod p)","-","-  // This is not a simple linear objective over the integers because of the mod operation.","-","-  // For a practical solution with the given constraints, let me limit the enumeration based","-  // on the product of modulus^numFree, and fall back to a heuristic or branch-and-bound","-  // for very large cases.","-","-  // Given the problem states \"up to 40 buttons and 40 counters, modulus up to 97, under 5 seconds\",","-  // I believe the test cases won't have both large modulus AND many free variables simultaneously.","-  // Let me set a reasonable limit on enumeration and use branch-and-bound for the rest.","-","-  const maxEnum = 2_000_000; // Max enumerations to attempt","-  const enumSize = Math.pow(modulus, numFree);","-  if (enumSize <= maxEnum) {","-    return solveCounterEnumerate(aug, numVars, rank, pivotCol, freeVars, modulus);","-  }","-","-  // Branch and bound: assign free variables one at a time, prune if lower bound exceeds best","-  const assignment = new Array(numVars).fill(0);","+  const freeAssign = new Int32Array(numFree);","+  const pivotPartial = new Int32Array(rhs); // Current partial pivot values (not yet modded)","   let best: number[] | null = null;","   let bestTotal = Infinity;"," ","-  // Precompute for each pivot: constant term and coefficients of free vars","-  // pivot[r] = (aug[r][numVars] - sum_j>col aug[r][j] * assignment[j]) mod p","-  // where col = pivotCol[r]","-","-  function computePivotsAndTotal(): { valid: boolean; total: number } {","-    for (let r = rank - 1; r >= 0; r--) {","-      const col = pivotCol[r];","-      let val = aug[r][numVars];","-      for (let j = col + 1; j < numVars; j++) {","-        val = mod(val - aug[r][j] * assignment[j], modulus);","+  function search(depth: number, freeSum: number): void {","+    if (depth === numFree) {","+      // Compute final pivot values","+      let pivotSum = 0;","+      for (let r = 0; r < rank; r++) {","+        pivotSum += mod(pivotPartial[r], modulus);","       }","-      assignment[col] = val;","-    }","+      const total = freeSum + pivotSum;"," ","-    // Verify (should always be valid after RREF + consistency check)","-    let total = 0;","-    for (let i = 0; i < numVars; i++) {","-      total += assignment[i];","-    }","-    return { valid: true, total };","-  }","+      if (total < bestTotal || (total === bestTotal && best !== null)) {","+        // Build full assignment","+        const assignment = new Array(numVars).fill(0);","+        for (let i = 0; i < numFree; i++) {","+          assignment[freeVars[i]] = freeAssign[i];","+        }","+        for (let r = 0; r < rank; r++) {","+          assignment[pivotCol[r]] = mod(pivotPartial[r], modulus);","+        }"," ","-  function lowerBound(depth: number, currentFreeSum: number): number {","-    // Current sum of assigned free vars + minimum possible sum of remaining free vars + minimum pivot sum","-    let minRemaining = 0;","-    for (let i = depth; i < numFree; i++) {","-      minRemaining += 0; // free var = 0 is minimum","-    }","-","-    // For pivot variables, estimate minimum contribution","-    // This is a rough lower bound; each pivot is at least 0","-    return currentFreeSum + minRemaining;","-  }","-","-  function search(depth: number, currentFreeSum: number): void {","-    if (depth === numFree) {","-      const { total } = computePivotsAndTotal();","-      if (total < bestTotal || (total === bestTotal && best !== null && lexLessArr(assignment, best))) {","-        best = assignment.slice();","-        bestTotal = total;","+        if (total < bestTotal || lexLessArr(assignment, best!)) {","+          best = assignment;","+          bestTotal = total;","+        }","       }","       return;","     }"," ","-    if (lowerBound(depth, currentFreeSum) >= bestTotal) return;","+    if (freeSum >= bestTotal) return; // Prune"," ","     const fv = freeVars[depth];","+    // Coefficient of this free variable in each pivot equation","+    const coeffOffset = depth; // Used as coeff[r * numFree + depth]","+","     for (let v = 0; v < modulus; v++) {","-      assignment[fv] = v;","-      search(depth + 1, currentFreeSum + v);","+      freeAssign[depth] = v;","+","+      // Update pivot partial values","+      for (let r = 0; r < rank; r++) {","+        pivotPartial[r] -= coeff[r * numFree + coeffOffset] * v;","+      }","+","+      search(depth + 1, freeSum + v);","+","+      // Restore pivot partial values","+      for (let r = 0; r < rank; r++) {","+        pivotPartial[r] += coeff[r * numFree + coeffOffset] * v;","+      }","     }","-    assignment[fv] = 0;","+    freeAssign[depth] = 0;","   }"," ","   search(0, 0);"]}],"originalFile":"export interface Machine {\n  target: boolean[];\n  buttons: number[][];\n}\n\n// --- GF(2) helpers ---\n\nfunction buildGF2Matrix(machine: Machine): {\n  aug: number[][];\n  numVars: number;\n  numEqs: number;\n} {\n  const numVars = machine.buttons.length;\n  const numEqs = machine.target.length;\n  // Augmented matrix: each row has numVars coefficients + 1 RHS\n  const aug: number[][] = [];\n  for (let eq = 0; eq < numEqs; eq++) {\n    const row = new Array(numVars + 1).fill(0);\n    for (let btn = 0; btn < numVars; btn++) {\n      if (machine.buttons[btn].includes(eq)) {\n        row[btn] = 1;\n      }\n    }\n    row[numVars] = machine.target[eq] ? 1 : 0;\n    aug.push(row);\n  }\n  return { aug, numVars, numEqs };\n}\n\nfunction rrefGF2(aug: number[][], numVars: number, numEqs: number): {\n  pivotCol: number[];\n  pivotRow: number[];\n  rank: number;\n} {\n  const pivotCol = new Array(numEqs).fill(-1);\n  const pivotRow = new Array(numVars).fill(-1);\n  let rank = 0;\n  let curRow = 0;\n\n  for (let col = 0; col < numVars && curRow < numEqs; col++) {\n    // Find pivot\n    let found = -1;\n    for (let row = curRow; row < numEqs; row++) {\n      if (aug[row][col] === 1) {\n        found = row;\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n    if (found === -1) continue;\n\n    // Swap rows\n    [aug[curRow], aug[found]] = [aug[found], aug[curRow]];\n    pivotCol[curRow] = col;\n    pivotRow[col] = curRow;\n    rank++;\n\n    // Eliminate\n    for (let row = 0; row < numEqs; row++) {\n      if (row !== curRow && aug[row][col] === 1) {\n        for (let j = 0; j <= numVars; j++) {\n          aug[row][j] ^= aug[curRow][j];\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    curRow++;\n  }\n\n  return { pivotCol, pivotRow, rank };\n}\n\n/**\n * Solve toggle puzzle using GF(2) Gaussian elimination.\n * For up to ~20 free variables, enumerate. For more, use meet-in-the-middle.\n */\nexport function solveToggle(machine: Machine): number[] | null {\n  const numVars = machine.buttons.length;\n  const numEqs = machine.target.length;\n\n  if (numVars === 0 && numEqs === 0) return [];\n  if (numEqs === 0) return [];\n  if (numVars === 0) {\n    return machine.target.some((t) => t) ? null : [];\n  }\n\n  const { aug, numVars: nv, numEqs: ne } = buildGF2Matrix(machine);\n  const { pivotCol, pivotRow, rank } = rrefGF2(aug, nv, ne);\n\n  // Check consistency: any row with all zeros on left but RHS=1\n  for (let row = rank; row < ne; row++) {\n    if (aug[row][nv] === 1) return null;\n  }\n\n  // Identify free variables (columns without pivots)\n  const freeVars: number[] = [];\n  for (let col = 0; col < nv; col++) {\n    if (pivotRow[col] === -1) freeVars.push(col);\n  }\n\n  const numFree = freeVars.length;\n\n  // If few enough free variables, enumerate all possibilities\n  if (numFree <= 20) {\n    return solveToggleEnumerate(aug, nv, rank, pivotCol, pivotRow, freeVars);\n  }\n\n  // Meet-in-the-middle for >20 free variables\n  return solveToggleMITM(machine, aug, nv, ne, rank, pivotCol, pivotRow, freeVars);\n}\n\nfunction solveToggleEnumerate(\n  aug: number[][],\n  numVars: number,\n  rank: number,\n  pivotCol: number[],\n  pivotRow: number[],\n  freeVars: number[],\n): number[] | null {\n  const numFree = freeVars.length;\n  let best: number[] | null = null;\n  let bestCount = Infinity;\n\n  for (let mask = 0; mask < (1 << numFree); mask++) {\n    const assignment = new Array(numVars).fill(0);\n\n    // Set free variables from mask\n    for (let i = 0; i < numFree; i++) {\n      assignment[freeVars[i]] = (mask >> i) & 1;\n    }\n\n    // Back-substitute pivot variables\n    for (let r = rank - 1; r >= 0; r--) {\n      const col = pivotCol[r];\n      let val = aug[r][numVars];\n      for (let j = col + 1; j < numVars; j++) {\n        if (aug[r][j] === 1) val ^= assignment[j];\n      }\n      assignment[col] = val;\n    }\n\n    const pressed: number[] = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < numVars; i++) {\n      if (assignment[i] === 1) pressed.push(i);\n    }\n\n    if (pressed.length < bestCount || (pressed.length === bestCount && lexLess(pressed, best!))) {\n      best = pressed;\n      bestCount = pressed.length;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return best;\n}\n\nfunction lexLess(a: number[], b: number[]): boolean {\n  for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(a.length, b.length); i++) {\n    if (a[i] < b[i]) return true;\n    if (a[i] > b[i]) return false;\n  }\n  return a.length < b.length;\n}\n\n/**\n * Meet-in-the-middle for toggle puzzle with many free variables.\n * Split free variables into two halves, enumerate each, match on pivot variable constraints.\n */\nfunction solveToggleMITM(\n  machine: Machine,\n  aug: number[][],\n  numVars: number,\n  _numEqs: number,\n  rank: number,\n  pivotCol: number[],\n  _pivotRow: number[],\n  freeVars: number[],\n): number[] | null {\n  const numFree = freeVars.length;\n  const half = Math.floor(numFree / 2);\n  const leftFree = freeVars.slice(0, half);\n  const rightFree = freeVars.slice(half);\n  const leftCount = leftFree.length;\n  const rightCount = rightFree.length;\n\n  // For each pivot variable, compute its expression as: pivot = rhs XOR (sum of free var contributions)\n  // We need to split the contribution into left and right halves.\n\n  // Build pivot expressions: for each pivot row, which free vars affect it?\n  // pivot = aug[row][numVars] XOR sum(free_vars_in_row)\n  // Split: pivot = rhs XOR leftContrib XOR rightContrib\n\n  interface HalfResult {\n    // For matching: the key is the vector of pivot variable values induced by this half\n    // (assuming r